        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 238.5,
          "end": 241.74,
          "en": "which could have unwanted side effects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.74,
          "end": 244.11,
          "en": "By setting this button to type=\"button\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.11,
          "end": 245.88,
          "en": "this will not occur.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.88,
          "end": 249.153,
          "en": "But that's just a side note, not specific to Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.74,
          "end": 253.05,
          "en": "Now, these click listeners on the Cancel button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.05,
          "end": 256.26,
          "en": "the backdrop, should invoke a method inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.26,
          "end": 257.973,
          "en": "of the new-task.component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.87,
          "end": 261.18,
          "en": "So in here in the component class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.18,
          "end": 264.57,
          "en": "we can add a new onCancel method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 264.57,
          "end": 269.22,
          "en": "And now I wanna emit a custom event whenever that happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 269.22,
          "end": 273.78,
          "en": "So as you learned it before, we should use @Output here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 273.78,
          "end": 277.74,
          "en": "which of course is imported from @angular/core as always.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 277.74,
          "end": 280.32,
          "en": "And then add our own event property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.32,
          "end": 284.58,
          "en": "which could be named cancel since this accurately describes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284.58,
          "end": 286.533,
          "en": "the kind of event we're adding here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 287.73,
          "end": 290.7,
          "en": "Now, this should be a new EventEmitter as always,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 290.7,
          "end": 292.713,
          "en": "imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.94,
          "end": 295.65,
          "en": "And this will be an EventEmitter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 295.65,
          "end": 298.89300000000003,
          "en": "that will actually not transmit any kind of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.90999999999997,
          "end": 302.55,
          "en": "Therefore, as a generic type annotation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 302.55,
          "end": 305.61,
          "en": "you should add the special void type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 305.61,
          "end": 308.34,
          "en": "Now, that is something you didn't know in advance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 308.34,
          "end": 309.84,
          "en": "but you could also set it up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 309.84,
          "end": 313.71,
          "en": "without any generic type information at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.71,
          "end": 316.71,
          "en": "Void is just a special type that essentially means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.71,
          "end": 320.31,
          "en": "that there will be no data being emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.31,
          "end": 323.34,
          "en": "And with that, we can then go here to onCancel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 323.34,
          "end": 325.38,
          "en": "and use our cancel property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 325.38,
          "end": 328.83299999999997,
          "en": "to emit a new event which does not carry any data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 330.39,
          "end": 333.75,
          "en": "And now with that, we can use this onCancel method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 333.75,
          "end": 336.84000000000003,
          "en": "in the new-task.component.html file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 336.84000000000003,
          "end": 339.57,
          "en": "both for the backdrop click listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 339.57,
          "end": 343.02,
          "en": "and this Cancel button click listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 343.02,
          "end": 347.07,
          "en": "And we can then use our own cancel event here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 347.07,
          "end": 351.87,
          "en": "so to say, in the tasks.component template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 351.87,
          "end": 353.88,
          "en": "to listen for that cancel event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 353.88,
          "end": 356.7,
          "en": "on the new-task.component instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 356.7,
          "end": 359.867,
          "en": "And then here we wanna invoke onCancelAddTask.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 360.81,
          "end": 364.05,
          "en": "This method we added a couple of minutes ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 364.05,
          "end": 366.6,
          "en": "If you now save everything, you should be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 366.6,
          "end": 370.47,
          "en": "to open this dialog, but to then also close it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 370.47,
          "end": 373.23,
          "en": "by clicking on the backdrop like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 373.23,
          "end": 375.723,
          "en": "or by clicking on the Cancel button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 377.07,
          "end": 380.79,
          "en": "And that's another important step into the right direction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 380.79,
          "end": 382.92,
          "en": "Next, we, of course, wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 382.92,
          "end": 385.71,
          "en": "that we also extract the entered data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 385.71,
